---
# An end state (everything loaded, nothing left to do but stutter) is
# not a deadlock; the liveness check still sees it.
deadlock_detection: false
---
# The control room's sidebar, client side: what the person sees in the
# session list and can do with it (go/tests/model/README.md).
#
# Code this is checked against (go/internal/serve/web/src):
#   app.tsx  Sidebar: closed (⌘B, side-collapse, the rail), searching +
#            query (the filter field, "/", Escape), wsFolded (a group's
#            fold), showArchived/archFolded/archFromFilter (Archived and
#            "Include"), dragging/dropAt + dropProject (drag a row onto a
#            project group), card (the hover card), the Seen button, the
#            unseen dot, the Needs you pins, the "No sessions" line.
#   app.tsx  App: refresh/loadedAt/loadErr (the list read), visible (the
#            query filter), pane (a phone shows list or thread), the
#            viewing ack (viewingUnseen), act() for Seen and the move.
#   status.tsx  sessionSignal/hasFailure/isUnseen (what pins and dots).
#
# The world: one local session A (a: "none" until it appears, then
# running/done/failed), a project p whose thread B may exist (proj), and
# one archived session Z, always in the store. A is what the person
# clicks, hovers, drags and marks seen; B is only there so p has a group
# to drop A on; Z is only there so Archived has something to load.
# Neither query the person types matches B or Z: "hit" matches A's title,
# "miss" matches nothing.
#
# Where this model differs from the surface as first mapped:
# - There is no filter MENU and no inline rename in the sidebar: the
#   filter is a text field behind the toolbar's Filter button (and "/"),
#   and rename lives in the thread header's popover (askText). Neither
#   rename nor a menu is modelled here.
# - The only per-row hover affordance is the hover card (after 300 ms,
#   closed by any pointerdown, scroll, blur or route change); the Seen
#   button is always shown on a troubled row, not only on hover.
# - A failed session is pinned under Needs you and, when it is a local
#   one, leaves its folder group (a group left empty is not drawn). It
#   stays pinned after Seen: sessionSignal ranks a recorded failure from
#   the last 72 h as needing you, seen or not; Seen only drops the button.
# - Moving is not optimistic: act() waits for POST assign, then re-reads
#   the list; until then the row stays in its folder (move "pending").
#   A project session (mode project) is not draggable at all, and a local
#   session already in p could only be dropped on its own folder's group,
#   which exists only with another row in it: not modelled (A moves in,
#   never out).
# - The first list read is "loading" (the page says so after 200 ms; the
#   harness clock is past that), "unavailable" when it fails. A later
#   read failing is "delayed": the rows stay under the notice.
# - Server events (a session appearing, a turn finishing or failing) are
#   the change plus the list read that shows it, so they need the list
#   readable (rows "ready"). One turn: A appears running and ends done
#   or failed; a second prompt adds states and no sidebar mechanism.
#
# Keeping it small: every path is one browser test, so each feature is
# exercised from a quiet state (no filter, Archived shut, no drag, the
# home route, a desktop) unless the code ties it to another one:
# - the filter with Archived ("Include" lasts as long as the filter), with
#   the rail and ⌘B (⌘B does nothing in the field), with Needs you (a
#   query unpins) and with the empty line ("No sessions match");
# - the unseen dot and the ack with the route, the rail and a phone's panes;
# - Needs you with the group fold, and with p's group after a move.
# So: the filter opens on a desktop's home route, before a finish and
# without trouble; Archived opens only before A appears (it is the empty
# line's other half); a phone only opens, leaves and acks (the filter,
# ⌘B, hover and drag are desktop's); server events wait while the filter
# or Archived is open. Not modelled: Escape in the tree (the field's
# Escape is), "/" from a phone's thread (it shows the list), ⌘B on a
# phone (it flips the saved flag the phone ignores), the per-search
# group folds, the turn log under a row, and arrow-key tree walking.
#
# All state lives in the Sidebar role (fizzbee-mbt compares role state).
# The last five fields are derived by recompute, the way the page derives
# them from the others. Every field is on the page: inField is
# document.activeElement being #q, closed is the side-collapse button's
# aria-expanded (in the DOM on a phone too, where CSS hides it).

role Sidebar:
    action Init:
        # "desktop" | "phone" (max-width:720px).
        self.viewport = "desktop"
        # A phone shows one pane: the list, or what the route opened.
        self.pane = "list"
        # "home" (#/), "session" (#/s/A), "page" (#/hooks: another view).
        self.route = "home"
        # bough:side-closed. Folds the sidebar to a rail on a desktop; a
        # phone hides the button and ignores it.
        self.closed = False
        # The filter: "off" (field hidden, no query), "open" (field shown,
        # query empty), "hit" (a query A matches), "miss" (one nothing
        # matches).
        self.search = "off"
        # Focus is in the filter field: typing goes to it, ⌘B and "/" do not.
        self.inField = False
        # The list read: "loading" | "unavailable" | "ready" | "delayed".
        self.rows = "loading"
        # Session A as the server has it.
        self.a = "none"
        self.unseen = False
        self.trouble = False
        # A's project: "" (listed under its folder) or "p".
        self.project = ""
        # Project p has a thread (B): p has a group in the sidebar.
        self.proj = False
        # A's folder group is folded (bough:ws-folded).
        self.groupFolded = False
        # Archived: "off" (showArchived false), "loading", "failed",
        # "open" (loaded, section open), "folded" (loaded, section shut).
        self.arch = "off"
        # Archived was included from a filter's "Include": it lasts as
        # long as that filter.
        self.archFromFilter = False
        # Dragging A: "none" | "dragging" | "over" (over p's group, the
        # drop hint shown) | "pending" (dropped; POST assign in flight).
        self.move = "none"
        # The hover card over A's row.
        self.card = False
        # --- derived ---
        # "full" | "rail" | "hidden" (a phone showing the thread pane).
        self.side = "full"
        # What the list says: "loading" | "unavailable" | "delayed" |
        # "empty" (No sessions yet.) | "nomatch" (No sessions match) |
        # "rows" | "archived" (only the Archived section's own pending
        # load; its failure is the list's, "delayed") | "rail" | "hidden".
        self.says = "loading"
        # Where A's row is on screen: "none" (not listed, or the sidebar
        # is not showing rows), "group", "pinned" (Needs you), "folded"
        # (listed under a folded group, not drawn).
        self.aRow = "none"
        # The unseen dot on A's row.
        self.dot = False
        # The Seen button on A's row.
        self.seenBtn = False
        self.recompute()

    atomic func recompute():
        if self.viewport == "phone":
            side = "full" if self.pane == "list" else "hidden"
        elif self.closed:
            side = "rail"
        else:
            side = "full"
        self.side = side
        q = self.search in ("hit", "miss")
        listed = self.a != "none" and self.search != "miss"
        where = "none"
        if listed and side == "full" and self.rows in ("ready", "delayed"):
            if self.a == "failed" and not q:
                where = "pinned"
            elif self.groupFolded and not q and self.project == "":
                where = "folded"
            else:
                where = "group"
        self.aRow = where
        drawn = where in ("group", "pinned")
        # The card is drawn from the listed rows (cardRow): a row the
        # filter or a fold takes away takes its card with it.
        self.card = self.card and drawn
        self.dot = drawn and self.a == "done" and self.unseen and self.route != "session"
        self.seenBtn = drawn and self.trouble
        # Z is in the rows once Archived has loaded, and filtered by a query.
        zListed = self.arch in ("open", "folded") and not q
        total = (1 if listed else 0) + (1 if self.proj and not q else 0) + (1 if zListed else 0)
        if side != "full":
            says = side
        elif self.rows == "unavailable":
            says = "unavailable"
        elif self.rows == "loading":
            says = "loading"
        elif self.rows == "delayed":
            says = "delayed"
        elif total > 0:
            says = "rows"
        elif self.arch in ("loading", "failed"):
            says = "archived"
        elif q:
            says = "nomatch"
        else:
            says = "empty"
        self.says = says

    # Clearing the query ends an Archived included from it (archFromFilter
    # effect on searchOn).
    atomic func queryCleared():
        if self.archFromFilter:
            self.archFromFilter = False
            self.arch = "off"

    # --- the list read ---------------------------------------------------

    atomic action Loaded:
        require self.rows == "loading"
        self.rows = "ready"
        self.recompute()

    atomic action LoadFail:
        require self.rows == "loading"
        self.rows = "unavailable"
        self.recompute()

    # "Sessions unavailable · Retry". The click takes focus out of the
    # filter field, as every click on the list does.
    atomic action Retry:
        require self.rows == "unavailable" and self.side == "full"
        self.rows = "loading"
        self.inField = False
        self.recompute()

    # A later poll fails: "Updates delayed · synced … ago"; rows stay.
    atomic action PollFail:
        require (self.rows == "ready" and self.a == "running" and
                 self.search == "off" and self.arch == "off" and
                 self.move == "none" and self.route == "home" and
                 self.viewport == "desktop" and not self.card and not self.closed and
                 not self.proj and not self.groupFolded)
        self.rows = "delayed"
        self.recompute()

    # Not while Archived's own read is failing or out: that read is the
    # list's (one request carries both), and its answer is ArchivedLoaded.
    atomic fair action PollOk:
        require self.rows == "delayed" and self.arch not in ("failed", "loading")
        self.rows = "ready"
        self.recompute()

    # --- the server ------------------------------------------------------

    # A session started elsewhere (the CLI, another tab) is listed.
    atomic action Appear:
        require (self.rows == "ready" and self.a == "none" and self.search == "off" and
                 self.arch == "off")
        self.a = "running"
        self.recompute()

    # A thread is started in project p: p's group appears.
    atomic action ProjectThread:
        require (self.rows == "ready" and not self.proj and self.search == "off" and
                 self.arch == "off" and self.move == "none" and
                 self.route == "home" and self.viewport == "desktop" and
                 not self.closed and not self.groupFolded and self.a == "running")
        self.proj = True
        self.recompute()

    atomic action Finish:
        require (self.rows == "ready" and self.a == "running" and self.search == "off"
                 and self.arch == "off" and self.move == "none" and not self.card
                 and (not self.proj or self.project == "p"))
        self.a = "done"
        self.unseen = True
        self.recompute()

    atomic action Fail:
        require (self.rows == "ready" and self.a == "running" and self.search == "off"
                 and self.arch == "off" and self.move == "none" and not self.card
                 and (not self.proj or self.project == "p"))
        self.a = "failed"
        self.trouble = True
        self.recompute()

    # The page acks an unseen finish on screen (viewingUnseen). Not the
    # trouble: that has Seen.
    atomic fair<strong> action AutoAck:
        require (self.unseen and self.route == "session" and
                 (self.viewport == "desktop" or self.pane == "thread"))
        self.unseen = False
        self.recompute()

    # --- rows -----------------------------------------------------------

    # Click A's row (in its group or its Needs you pin). From the home
    # route only, so Back always lands on home (see Back).
    atomic action OpenRow:
        require (self.aRow in ("group", "pinned") and self.move == "none" and
                 self.route == "home" and self.search in ("off", "hit") and
                 self.arch == "off" and (not self.proj or self.project == "p"))
        self.route = "session"
        self.pane = "thread"
        self.inField = False
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    # Back home. A page's own Back (page-head .back, goList) on either
    # viewport and the phone thread's (thread-head .back, goList); on a
    # desktop the thread's Back is hidden, and it is the sidebar's history
    # arrow, which returns to #/ because OpenRow only leaves from there.
    atomic action Back:
        require (self.route != "home" and
                 (self.viewport == "desktop" or self.pane == "thread"))
        self.route = "home"
        self.pane = "list"
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    # A page beside sessions from the sidebar's nav (Hooks).
    atomic action NavPage:
        require (self.search == "off" and self.arch == "off" and
                 self.move == "none" and self.route == "home" and
                 self.viewport == "desktop" and self.side == "full" and
                 not self.card and self.a in ("none", "running") and not self.proj)
        self.route = "page"
        self.pane = "thread"
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    # The hover card, 300 ms after the pointer rests on A's row.
    atomic action Hover:
        require (self.aRow in ("group", "pinned") and not self.card and
                 self.search == "off" and self.arch == "off" and
                 self.move == "none" and self.route == "home" and
                 self.viewport == "desktop" and self.rows == "ready" and
                 not self.proj and self.a in ("running", "failed"))
        self.card = True
        self.recompute()

    atomic action Unhover:
        require self.card
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    # Seen on a troubled row: act(api.ack), then the list re-read.
    atomic action MarkSeen:
        require self.seenBtn and self.move == "none"
        self.trouble = False
        self.card = False
        self.inField = False
        self.recompute()

    # A's folder group's head (a folder has no page: its whole head folds).
    atomic action FoldGroup:
        require (self.aRow in ("group", "folded") and self.project == "" and
                 self.search == "off" and self.arch == "off" and
                 self.move == "none" and self.route == "home" and
                 self.viewport == "desktop" and not self.proj and
                 self.a in ("running", "done"))
        self.groupFolded = not self.groupFolded
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    # --- drag and drop ---------------------------------------------------

    atomic action DragStart:
        require (self.aRow == "group" and self.project == "" and
                 self.search == "off" and self.arch == "off" and
                 self.move == "none" and self.route == "home" and
                 self.viewport == "desktop" and self.rows == "ready" and
                 self.a == "running")
        self.move = "dragging"
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    # Over p's group: dropProject says A moves to p; the hint shows.
    atomic action DragOver:
        require self.move == "dragging" and self.proj
        self.move = "over"
        self.recompute()

    atomic action DragLeave:
        require self.move == "over"
        self.move = "dragging"
        self.recompute()

    # Let go anywhere that takes no drop.
    atomic action DragCancel:
        require self.move in ("dragging", "over")
        self.move = "none"
        self.recompute()

    atomic action Drop:
        require self.move == "over"
        self.move = "pending"
        self.recompute()

    atomic fair action MoveOk:
        require self.move == "pending"
        self.move = "none"
        self.project = "p"
        self.groupFolded = False
        self.recompute()

    # Refused (the error bar says why); the row stays in its folder.
    atomic action MoveFail:
        require self.move == "pending"
        self.move = "none"
        self.recompute()

    # --- collapse --------------------------------------------------------

    # ⌘B, or the toolbar's panel button: never from inside the field.
    atomic action ToggleSide:
        require (self.viewport == "desktop" and not self.inField and
                 self.move == "none" and self.arch == "off" and
                 self.route in ("home", "session") and not self.groupFolded and
                 not self.proj and self.rows == "ready" and self.search != "miss")
        self.closed = not self.closed
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    # The rail's Filter button: unfold with the field open. Focus comes
    # from the effect on `searching` turning true, so it lands in the
    # field only when the field was shut: a field left open (a query in
    # force when the list was folded) comes back unfocused.
    atomic action RailFilter:
        require (self.side == "rail" and self.route == "home" and self.a != "done" and
                 not self.trouble)
        self.closed = False
        if self.search == "off":
            self.search = "open"
            self.inField = True
        self.recompute()

    # The window crosses 720 px. A field the new layout hides loses focus.
    atomic action Resize:
        require (self.search == "off" and self.arch == "off" and self.move == "none" and not self.card
                 and self.route != "page" and self.rows == "ready" and not self.closed
                 and not self.groupFolded and not self.proj)
        self.viewport = "phone" if self.viewport == "desktop" else "desktop"
        self.recompute()

    # --- the filter ------------------------------------------------------

    # "/" anywhere not typing: unfold, show the list (a phone), focus.
    atomic action Slash:
        require (not self.inField and self.move == "none" and self.arch == "off" and
                 self.route == "home" and self.viewport == "desktop" and
                 not self.groupFolded and not self.proj and not self.card and
                 self.a != "done" and not self.trouble)
        self.closed = False
        self.pane = "list"
        if self.search == "off":
            self.search = "open"
        self.inField = True
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    # The toolbar's Filter button: opens the field, or clears and hides it.
    atomic action FilterButton:
        require (self.side == "full" and self.move == "none" and
                 self.route == "home" and self.viewport == "desktop" and
                 not self.groupFolded and not self.proj and not self.card and
                 self.a != "done" and not self.trouble)
        if self.search == "off":
            self.search = "open"
            self.inField = True
        else:
            self.search = "off"
            self.inField = False
            self.queryCleared()
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    atomic action TypeHit:
        require self.inField and self.search != "hit" and self.viewport == "desktop"
        self.search = "hit"
        self.recompute()

    atomic action TypeMiss:
        require self.inField and self.search != "miss" and self.viewport == "desktop"
        self.search = "miss"
        self.recompute()

    # Delete the query; the field stays.
    atomic action ClearQuery:
        require self.inField and self.search in ("hit", "miss")
        self.search = "open"
        self.queryCleared()
        self.recompute()

    # Escape in the field: clear, hide, focus back on the Filter button.
    atomic action Escape:
        require self.inField
        self.search = "off"
        self.inField = False
        self.queryCleared()
        self.recompute()

    # --- Archived ---------------------------------------------------------

    # The section's header: off opens and loads it ("Include" under a
    # query, which ties it to the query); loaded, it folds and unfolds.
    atomic action ArchivedHead:
        # "Opened and empty, the fold has nothing to offer" never hides
        # the header here: Z is always there.
        require (self.side == "full" and self.rows == "ready"
                 and (self.arch == "off" or (self.arch in ("open", "folded") and self.search == "off"))
                 and self.move == "none" and self.route == "home" and self.viewport == "desktop"
                 and not self.groupFolded and not self.proj and not self.card and self.a == "none")
        if self.arch == "off":
            self.arch = "loading"
            self.archFromFilter = self.search in ("hit", "miss")
        elif self.arch == "open":
            self.arch = "folded"
        else:
            self.arch = "open"
        self.inField = False
        self.card = False
        self.recompute()

    atomic fair action ArchivedLoaded:
        require self.arch == "loading"
        self.arch = "open"
        self.rows = "ready"
        self.recompute()

    # Archived is read with the list, in one request: its failure is the
    # list's too, and the list says its updates are delayed.
    atomic action ArchivedFail:
        require self.arch == "loading" and self.search == "off"
        self.arch = "failed"
        self.rows = "delayed"
        self.recompute()

    # "Couldn't load archived · Retry". The retry is the list's read
    # again: while it is out, neither says it failed.
    atomic action ArchivedRetry:
        require self.arch == "failed" and self.side == "full"
        self.arch = "loading"
        self.rows = "ready"
        self.inField = False
        self.recompute()

action Init:
    sidebar = Sidebar()

# Focus in the filter field means the field is on screen.
always assertion FieldFocusNeedsField:
    return not sidebar.inField or (sidebar.search != "off" and sidebar.side == "full")

# The hover card belongs to a row on screen and never outlives a drag.
always assertion CardOverDrawnRow:
    return not sidebar.card or (sidebar.aRow in ("group", "pinned") and sidebar.move == "none")

# The open row carries no unseen dot (its ack is already on the way),
# and a dot only ever says a clean finish.
always assertion NoDotOnOpenRowOrFailure:
    return not sidebar.dot or (sidebar.route != "session" and sidebar.a == "done")

# Seen is offered only where marking seen does something.
always assertion SeenOnlyOnTrouble:
    return not sidebar.seenBtn or (sidebar.trouble and sidebar.a == "failed")

# "No sessions yet." only when there is nothing to list.
always assertion EmptyMeansNothing:
    return sidebar.says != "empty" or (sidebar.a == "none" and not sidebar.proj and sidebar.arch not in ("open", "folded"))

# A failure is never out of sight in the list: pinned whenever the
# sidebar shows rows unfiltered, whatever its group's fold.
always assertion FailurePinned:
    shown = sidebar.side == "full" and sidebar.rows in ("ready", "delayed") and sidebar.search in ("off", "open")
    return not (shown and sidebar.a == "failed") or sidebar.aRow == "pinned"

# A drop is offered only where it lands: a local session over a project
# group that exists.
always assertion DropOnlyWhereItLands:
    return sidebar.move not in ("over", "pending") or (sidebar.project == "" and sidebar.proj and sidebar.side == "full")

# Archived included from a filter lasts as long as that filter.
always assertion IncludeLastsWithFilter:
    return not sidebar.archFromFilter or sidebar.search in ("hit", "miss")

# The list always says something while it is on screen.
always assertion ListSaysSomething:
    return sidebar.side != "full" or sidebar.says in ("loading", "unavailable", "delayed", "empty", "nomatch", "rows", "archived")

# ⌘B never fires from inside the filter field (it is text editing there).
transition assertion NoFoldFromField(before, after):
    return before.sidebar.closed == after.sidebar.closed or not before.sidebar.inField

# An unseen finish on screen is acked: no run stays viewing it unseen.
always eventually assertion ViewedFinishIsAcked:
    s = sidebar
    return not (s.unseen and s.route == "session" and (s.viewport == "desktop" or s.pane == "thread"))
